gs and put a  restaurant inside of them but if I were  late paths to the  the guests were just completely clipped  through the past year with their feeds  which is something which doesn't really  look too good though looking back at  that some of the guests are currently  walking through walls which isn't too  great either so I might one is still do  it in the future but I don't think so  not much of a chance that I'm actually  gonna make this part of your building  over here actually functional that said  though I think that very narrow one tile  blue building might actually be good for  a restaurant at some point in the future  so may want to get back to that and the  rest of this building is really quite  similar to what I already have and I  also still had some shots which I  recorded as almost the flying camera  though these aren't quite as good I do  have to say by the way I recorded these  shots not with any speak not any  spectacular camera function or something  that other people don't have I just sort  of hooked that I just sort of changed  the camera settings the key settings of  the camera to minus 10 when it comes to  the movement and then started spamming  the a and D keys on my keyboard which  was a absolute pain but it actually did  result in some really cool videos though  they are slightly sped up because yeah  lag is still a bit of an issue for me  and it's definitely parts of the fact  that this park is pretty large the game  is of course they want alpha as well and  I don't have the very best computer but  it's one reason why I am a little bit  hesitant to try more life or real-time  parts and here you can also kind of see  it jittering a bit but that is  completely my mistake and in very I was  really good at tapping the keyboard at  this point in time but yeah this is  pretty much what the Main Street looks  like and more of a battery close-up of  what each individual building is  actually like I kind of like it so far  but there is still quite a lot to be  worked on especially a new building  which might actually be my favorite  building of the Main Street so far and  also adding some extra details and  actually doing a bit of backstage area  to make everything look a little bit  realistic but yeah that's all for the  next episode so thank you guys for  watching and I'll see you guys next time
 

